#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:2
msgid "Upgrade Team Edition to Enterprise Edition"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:4
msgid ""
"If you're evaluating Mattermost using Team Edition, you'll need to "
"upgrade to Mattermost Enterprise Edition before you can start a trial or "
"upload a license that enables Enterprise features. The open source "
"Mattermost Team Edition is functionally identical to the commercial "
"Enterprise Edition, but there is no ability to start a trial or unlock "
"paid features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:7
msgid "Upgrade to Enterprise Edition"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:10
msgid "Check your edition and version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:12
msgid ""
"Open **Product menu > About Mattermost** to check your edition and "
"version from the web or desktop interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:14
msgid ""
"**Mattermost Entry** indicates you're using the licensed edition of "
"Mattermost without a paid license."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:15
msgid ""
"**Mattermost Professional** indicates you're using the licensed edition "
"of Mattermost with a paid professional license."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:16
msgid ""
"**Mattermost Enterprise** indicates you're using the licensed edition of "
"Mattermost with a paid enterprise license."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:17
msgid ""
"**Mattermost Enterprise Advanced** indicates you're using the licensed "
"edition of Mattermost with a paid enterprise advanced license."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:18
msgid ""
"**Mattermost Team Edition** indicates you're using the open source "
"version and need to upgrade to a licensed edition before a license key "
"can be applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:21
msgid "Upgrade via System Console (Recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:23
msgid ""
"Most standalone servers can upgrade Team Edition to Enterprise Edition in"
" minutes using the built-in conversion tool in the System Console, and "
"this is our recommended approach."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:25
msgid ""
"Go to **Product menu > System Console > Edition and License** and select "
"**Upgrade to Enterprise Edition**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:27
msgid ""
"During the upgrade process, the Mattermost Enterprise Edition binary file"
" that matches your current server version is downloaded, decompressed, "
"and extracted. The Team Edition binary is then replaced by the Enterprise"
" Edition version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:30
msgid ""
"If you're using a modified version of Mattermost, using this tool will "
"overwrite your changes and replace them with the official Enterprise "
"Edition binary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:32
msgid ""
"Once this process is complete, you're prompted to restart your server. "
"The Mattermost version listed in **Product menu > System Console > "
"Edition and License** will change from **Team Edition** to **Mattermost "
"Entry**, and you can now upload a professional, enterprise, or enterprise"
" advanced license to unlock paid features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:35
msgid "Upgrade manually"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:37
msgid ""
"You can alternatively replace the Mattermost Team Edition binary with a "
"Mattermost Enterprise Edition binary when running a regularly scheduled "
"server upgrade via this :doc:`upgrade procedure </administration-"
"guide/upgrade/upgrading-mattermost-server>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/upgrade/enterprise-install-upgrade.rst:39
msgid ""
"We recommend backing up Mattermost prior to upgrading. The "
":doc:`migration guide </administration-guide/onboard/migrating-to-"
"mattermost>` documentation outlines the process required to back up and "
"restore your database."
msgstr ""

